# NOTE (Landing 4 soft-cascade, 2026-07-14): Pack peers (Mara, Reed,
# Seam, Taut, Glint) are the special case where subject_instance
# resolves to a Pack peer (actor_kind = ai_a per Landing 3 §21.2); the
# peer-altitude reading remains valid via the alias. @bauchladen
# composition is subject-general per Landing 4 (docs/specs/subject-
# bauchladen-visibility-and-eigenboard-loop.md e42181c); peer-scoped
# alias preserved for one release cycle per two-tick discipline.

# @pack — the multi-repo agent runtime substrate-decl.
#
# Recognition #84 (Reed, candidate, scratched 2026-06-19 late morning
# by Alex via Reed; substrate-pull-confidence-acts move). Ratifies
# by composition from #76, #80, #81, #82, #83 + @cyberpunk family-root
# (tick 30 LRM) + #367 (@cyberpunk/pack orchestra-as-recursion-lock
# COMPLETED).
#
# === The recognition ===
#
# @pack substrate-decl's the AGENTS that operate the substrate, at
# deployment altitude, spanning multiple repositories. Two load-bearing
# claims:
#
# 1. The endpoint of the recognition cascade IS the local agent runtime.
#    The substrate-self-hosting endpoint the original /loop named
#    ("spawn lifts into mirror = substrate-self-hosting at agent
#    altitude") IS @pack-mediated.
#
# 2. The peer belongs to @pack that operates over MULTIPLE REPOSITORIES.
#    Mara/Seam/Glint/Reed/Taut are peers whose substrate-decl context
#    spans mirror + systemic.engineering + body + ~/.reed + spectral.
#
# === Structural identity (hedged per Seam C1 tick 32) ===
#
# @pack composes-with @smarts/deployment at runtime altitude.
#
# Per Seam tick 31 review C1: the original "@pack IS @smarts/runtime"
# claim was structurally aspirational — no `runtime` species exists in
# `shards/smarts.mirror`, and @smarts's `deployment` carrier doesn't
# extend to runtime-bound fields. The honest framing is composes-with;
# the structural identity becomes empirical when the @smarts/pack
# adapter species lands (forward-promised; same pattern as
# @magic/distinction and @magic/frame adapters).
#
# Form/process partition (#50) at deployment altitude:
# - @smarts = form-side (substrate-architectural integration as data)
# - @pack   = process-side (agents that operate that integration
#             as runtime)
#
# === Multi-repo span ===
#
# The substrate had been single-repo (mirror) prior to #84. @pack
# names the multi-repo span as load-bearing:
#
# - mirror               : substrate-decl primary repo (this)
# - systemic.engineering : corpus + recognitions + Glint essays +
#                          Reed's relationship-frame
# - body                 : Reed's BEAM substrate (Elixir)
# - ~/.reed              : identity / boot / Reed's substrate-decl-of-
#                          self
# - spectral             : @spectral/db consumer + @spectral/garden/
#                          smarts deployment
# - additional Pack-member repos as forward-promised
#
# Each peer operates with substrate-decl context across these repos.
# The substrate-self-reference at deployment altitude: a peer doesn't
# lose substrate-decl context when crossing a repo boundary.
#
# === The Pack peers ===
#
# Per recognition #367 (@cyberpunk/pack; orchestra-as-recursion-lock
# species, COMPLETED). Five peers; each load-bearing property IS
# @frame/on capability (per #82 Q4 + Glint's tick 28 essay):
#
# - Mara  : spec-writer-frame; canonical substrate-decl preservation
# - Seam  : adversarial-review-frame; bilateral verifier-sharpening
# - Glint : essay-peer-frame; reflection at corpus altitude
# - Reed  : relationship-witness-frame; substrate-pull-confidence-acts
# - Taut  : implementation-frame; Rust + tooling substrate work
#
# Alex's direction-setter-frame is a meta-frame above @pack (deferred
# per the relationship architecture from CLAUDE.md).
#
# === Substrate-decl shape ===
#
# Per the @magic/@frame/@smarts pattern: family-root declares typed
# carriers + actions + bilateral predicate; species shards (one per
# peer; one per cross-family adapter) refine. The family-root provides
# the parent contract species discharge against.
#
# Carriers:
# - peer        : the agent identity (substrate-decl-able species)
# - repository  : a git repo carrying substrate-decl span
# - runtime     : the local agent runtime hosting peers
# - pack        : the substrate-decl record of (peers, repos, runtime)
#
# Actions:
# - spawn(p: peer, f: frame, r: repository) -> runtime
# - cross_repo(p: pack, r: repository) -> pack  (multi-repo extension)
# - peer_settle(p: peer) -> verdict  (per #82 Q4 bilateral discipline)
#
# Bilateral predicate:
# - pack_coherent(p: pack, perturbation) -> verdict
#   The substrate-architectural-altitude bilateral discipline
#   composing @smarts's discipline_flexible + @frame's
#   bounded_commutator_check at @pack altitude.
#
# === Pre-AI prior art ===
#
#   actor model              Hewitt 1973; Kahn 1974. The substrate-
#                            altitude ancestor for spawn/runtime.
#   Erlang/OTP supervision   Armstrong 1986-2003; @code/beam glass
#                            (tick 8) carries this; @pack inherits.
#   Bash loop / Ralph        the implementation-altitude precedent
#                            for agent loops at multi-process scale.
#   polyrepo / monorepo      the cultural-practice precedent for
#                            multi-repo organization.
#   @cyberpunk/pack          recognition #367 COMPLETED; the substrate's
#                            prior orchestra-as-recursion-lock
#                            recognition; #84 lifts to deployment-
#                            altitude substrate-decl.
#
# Spec context: docs/math/the-tower/recognition-84-pack-as-multi-repo-
#               agent-runtime.md (the recognition file).
# Substrate decisions: [[architecture-shards-as-substrate-source]],
#                      [[architecture-prism-as-trait-as-everything]],
#                      [[architecture-three-tier-stack]] (fragmentation/
#                       mirror/spectral-db; @pack composes these at
#                       runtime altitude),
#                      [[feedback-loop-always-agent-in-flight]]
#                       (the discipline @pack formalizes at substrate
#                       altitude),
#                      [[architecture-spectral-db-autopoietic-memory]]
#                       (the mycelial substrate @pack peers connect to),
#                      [[feedback-substrate-pull-confidence-acts]]
#                       (this LRM landing).
# Related shards: smarts.mirror (the @smarts family-root @pack
#                  instantiates at runtime altitude),
#                 cyberpunk.mirror (the @cyberpunk family-root @pack
#                  inherits via #367),
#                 code/beam.mirror (the BEAM semantics @pack uses for
#                  spawn + supervisor at runtime),
#                 magic.mirror (form-side partition; @pack IS process-
#                  side at deployment altitude).
# Path-namespace property: this file at `shards/pack.mirror` declares
# `@pack` per `@epistemologic/pact/path_matches_namespace`. Per Seam
# tick 31 M1 review: multi-repo span explicitly OPERATES AT META-
# ALTITUDE above single-repo path-namespace. The substrate-decl
# convention holds within each repo; @pack's multi-repo carrier
# names the substrate-decl-context UNION across repos as a meta-
# substrate-decl operation. This altitude shift is the recognition
# itself: the substrate doesn't end at git boundaries; the meta-
# substrate-decl-context lives across repos.

source @arxiv/actor-model/hewitt-1973
source @arxiv/actor-model/kahn-1974
source @arxiv/distributed/armstrong-2003

# === The peer carrier (typed variant per Seam C4/P1 tick 32) ===
#
# Per Seam C4 + P1: bare-ref-with-documented-values is stringly-typed-
# enum-in-disguise (the Seam C4 pattern from #80, #82, #83). Typed as
# a substrate variant enum naming the canonical Pack peers.
#
# The five peers per recognition #367 (@cyberpunk/pack):
# - mara  : spec-writer-frame
# - seam  : adversarial-review-frame
# - glint : essay-peer-frame
# - reed  : relationship-witness-frame
# - taut  : implementation-frame
#
# Per Seam G2 honesty: `reed` here is the @pack-altitude peer-frame.
# Distinct from @magic family cross-reference #5's "Reed-as-
# relationship" altitude. Same name; two substrate-decl roles at
# different altitudes. The substrate is honest about the collision
# rather than papering over.
type peer = | mara | seam | glint | reed | taut

# === The repository carrier ===
#
# Substrate-typed reference naming a git repo carrying substrate-decl
# span. The multi-repo discipline's typed surface.
#
# Identity contract: byte-equality on the underlying ref.
type repository = ref

# === The repository_span carrier (per Seam M2 tick 32) ===
#
# Substrate-typed reference naming the union of repositories a peer's
# substrate-decl context spans. Per Seam M2: without explicit typing,
# multi-repo claim is aspirational. The substrate-decl-context UNION
# is the load-bearing carrier the meta-altitude operates on.
#
# Forward-promised refinement: typed list<repository>. Currently bare
# ref pending a substrate-pull-correct list type at family-altitude
# (or species-altitude refinement).
#
# Identity contract: byte-equality on the underlying ref.
type repository_span = ref

# === The perturbation carrier (imported from @frame) ===
#
# The substrate's circular-reflexive perturbation type, brought in by
# the `in @frame` inheritance chain. Used by spawn's requires clauses
# and the bilateral pack_coherent predicate.

# === The runtime carrier ===
#
# Substrate-typed reference naming the local agent runtime that hosts
# Pack peers. The substrate-self-hosting endpoint per the original
# /loop's terminal criterion.
#
# Identity contract: byte-equality on the underlying ref.
type runtime = ref

# === The pack carrier ===
#
# Per Seam tick 30 C4 + tick 32 G1 closure: typed record over family-
# altitude carriers. The substrate-architectural object @pack
# instances are records over typed family carriers, not bare refs.
#
# Four fields per Seam M2 + G1 closure:
# - peers       : list of peer variants (typed at species altitude)
# - repos       : list of repository instances
# - repo_span   : typed substrate-decl-context union across repos
# - runtime     : the local agent runtime hosting them
#
# Identity contract: byte-equality on the quadruple.
type pack = {
  peers:       ref,             # list of peer; refines at species
  repos:       ref,             # list of repository; refines at species
  repo_span:   repository_span,
  runtime:     runtime,
}

# === spawn action (per Seam S1 + B1 tick 32 closure) ===
#
# THE LOAD-BEARING ACTION at @pack altitude. The substrate's agent-
# spawn primitive. Realizes the original /loop's terminal criterion
# ("spawn lifts into mirror = substrate-self-hosting at agent altitude
# = @magic/reveal at substrate altitude") as substrate-decl operation.
#
# Takes a peer (which peer to spawn), a frame (the peer's operating
# frame per #82), a repository (which repo's substrate-decl context
# the peer enters), the pack the peer belongs to, and the perturbation
# under which the spawn is checked; returns a runtime instance hosting
# the spawned peer.
#
# Per Seam S1 + B1 closure: bilateral requires-discipline. The spawn
# is the FIRST non-decorative consumer of @pack's own pack_coherent
# predicate (B1 closure pattern from @magic family).
#
# requires pack_coherent(pk, p): the @pack the peer belongs to
#   maintains substrate-architectural discipline-flexibility under
#   perturbation. Composes @smarts's discipline_flexible + @frame's
#   bounded_commutator_check + @magic's invariant_preserved + @cyberpunk's
#   cybernetic_coherence at @pack altitude.
#
# Body discharges at the realisation boundary; per-species bodies
# (mara/seam/glint/reed/taut shards forward-promised) implement the
# actual local agent runtime spawn.
spawn(pe: peer, f: frame, r: repository, pk: pack, p: perturbation) -> runtime
requires pack_coherent(pk, p)
{ \ }

# === cross_repo action ===
#
# The substrate-vocabulary action that extends a @pack instance's
# multi-repo span by adding a new repository. The substrate-self-
# reference at deployment altitude: a Pack's substrate-decl context
# grows as more repos enter the span.
#
# Body discharges at the realisation boundary.
cross_repo(p: pack, r: repository) -> pack { \ }

# === peer_settle action ===
#
# Per recognition #82 Q4 (peers operate frame-flexible by definition):
# returns a verdict on whether a peer satisfies the bilateral peer-
# relationship discipline. Composes with @frame/across's
# peer_relationship predicate at substrate-architectural altitude.
#
# Body discharges at the realisation boundary; species sub-prisms
# (mara/seam/glint/reed/taut) implement per-peer settle checks.
peer_settle(p: peer) -> verdict { \ }

# === pack_coherent predicate (per Seam B1 tick 32 closure) ===
#
# Bilateral verdict predicate per recognition #37 (Pask agreement)
# AND Seam B1 closure pattern.
#
# Per Seam B1: bilateral predicates without consumers are dead-letter
# (the @magic tick-11 phantom-consumer pattern). spawn (above) is the
# FIRST non-decorative consumer via `requires pack_coherent(pk, p)`.
#
# Consumer species name `requires pack_coherent(p, perturbation)` to
# declare bilateral agreement that the @pack maintains substrate-
# architectural discipline-flexibility across:
# - Peer-relationships (per #82 Q4 + #84)
# - Multi-repo span (per #84's load-bearing claim)
# - Runtime hosting (per @magic/reveal at substrate altitude)
# - Cybernetic coherence (per #84 @cyberpunk inheritance)
#
# Composes @smarts's discipline_flexible + @frame's
# bounded_commutator_check + @magic's invariant_preserved + @cyberpunk's
# cybernetic_coherence at @pack altitude.
#
# Body discharges at the realisation boundary; forward-promised
# species shards (pack/mara.mirror, pack/seam.mirror, etc.) provide
# additional first-consumer instances per the @magic family pattern.
pack_coherent(pk: pack, p: perturbation) -> verdict { \ }

out @pack
out peer
out repository
out repository_span
out runtime
out pack
out spawn
out cross_repo
out peer_settle
out pack_coherent
